* YOU SHOULD NOT USE ARRAY_FILTER TO REMOVE NULLS FOR NULLABLE COLUMNS, LEAVE THEM THERE SINCE IT'S NOT A RAW DB INSERT;
* IF NEED TO FILTER THE LISTS FOR ANY OTHER REASON THAT'S IS NOT NULLISH REMOVAL, THEN USE COLLECTION'S METHODS OR ARRAY_VALUES/ARRAY_COLUMNS TO ENSURE SHAPE CONSISTENCY;
* You NEED to ensure "break out" strategies for excessive attempting while loops;
* Always create a Symfony Console output instance for detailing the variation created;
* QUERIES FOR READING ONLY SHOULD BE OPTIMIZED WITH RAW SQL METHODS;
* BE EXTREMELY CAREFUL WITH DECODING WHEN CALLING insert() OR RAW DB METHODS (any that skips the Model's $casts and ::boted);
* FOR unique() OR CONTEXTUALLY IMPORTANT UNIQUINE COLUMNS (even though not constrained as such) FOR THE MOCKS, RUN A do/while CHECKING IF THE QUERY RETURNS POSITIVE FOR EXISTS;
* Create a private instance of the Symfony Console Output and call writeln for it right before saving/creating with a brief detail of the created variation;
* For every while loop, create an attempt limit to "break free" from excessive abnormal number of attempts;
* Always ensure a minimum amount of iterations per entity in the main loop (ex.: if the looping demands subtypes and types, then ensure at least 1 iteration foreach possible subtype and 1 iteration for each possible type);
* The number of final entities should be in the order of power of 2 {log(count(ENTITY), 2) % 1 === 0} to ensure better distribution on relational constraints;
* Ensure a clock limiter (the seeder cannot be running for more than X seconds, default 600s for financial/criticals modules, else 300s for others) to avoid infinite loops on complex relational constraints;
* Always ensure a HardCap limiter (the seeder cannot attempt more than X times overall, default 512 * [1-6], with the range being defined by how critical and complex the module is) to avoid infinite loops on complex relational constraints;
* Use the ErrorHandler helper for catching and logging exceptions on the seeder operations:
namespace App\Helpers;

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;

class ErrorHandler
{
	/**
	 * Evaluate if candidate error exists in data aggregator and log to appropriate channel
	 * 
	 * @param array $dataAggregator Reference to the error collection array
	 * @param array $candidate The candidate error to check and potentially add
	 * @param string $secondaryChannel Log level for duplicate messages (default: 'debug')
	 * @param string $mainChannel Log level for new unique errors (default: 'warning')
	 * @return void
	 */
	public static function evaluateExistenceToLogChannel(
		array &$dataAggregator,
		array $candidate,
		string $secondaryChannel = 'debug',
		string $mainChannel = 'warning',
		?string $seed = null
	): void {
		try {
			if (!isset($candidate['message'])) {
				Log::error('ErrorHandler::evaluateExistenceToLogChannel - Candidate missing required "message" key', [
					'candidate' => $candidate,
				]);
				return;
			}
			$context = $candidate['context'] ?? [];
			$message = $candidate['message'];
			if (\in_array($candidate, $dataAggregator, true)) {
				!empty($seed) && Log::debug("{$seed} failed");
				return;
			}
			$existingMessages = \array_column($dataAggregator, 'message');
			$messageExists = \in_array($message, $existingMessages, true);
			if (!(method_exists(Log::class, $mainChannel) && is_callable(Log::class, $mainChannel)))
				$mainChannel = 'warning';
			if (!(method_exists(Log::class, $secondaryChannel) && is_callable(Log::class, $secondaryChannel)))
				$secondaryChannel = 'debug';
			if ($messageExists)
				Log::$secondaryChannel($message, $context);
			else
				Log::$mainChannel($message, $context);
			$dataAggregator[] = $candidate;
		} catch (\Throwable $e) {
			Log::error('ErrorHandler::evaluateExistenceToLogChannel - Failed to process error', [
				'error' => $e->getMessage(),
				'candidate' => $candidate ?? null,
			]);
		}
	}
}

